#     corners_deg: [-0.706, -0.253, -0.19, -1.133, -0.938, -0.657, -0.348, -0.498]
#     corners_grid_deg: [-0.575, -0.122, -0.058, -1.001, -0.807, -0.525, -0.217, -0.366]
#     crota2_deg: -0.1315
#     description: The orientation of the field stop as the pointing figure of Parker et al. (2022) gives it, for comparison.  pixels
#       are the eight corners picked by hand on its Level-3 O V image, (x, y) in Level-3 pixels; that image is on the pixel grid of AIA
#       304 offset by 300 pixels in each axis, and its coordinates leave out AIA's own roll, crota2_deg (the CROTA2 of the AIA 304 images
#       of the flight).  corners_deg is each corner's departure from its nominal multiple of 45 degrees about their centroid, by nominal
#       azimuth 0, 45, ..., 315, on the sky with that roll, and corners_grid_deg the same on the AIA pixel grid without it, computed with
#       the full WCS of the AIA 304 image at 2019-09-30T18:08:43Z.  level3_rotation_deg is the rotation of each camera's image against
#       the AIA pixel grid in that paper's Level-3 co-alignment, the median over its sequences of the affine rot_angle in ov_Level3_transform.pickle
